   {
    "id": "1558145852183654118",
    "created_at": "2025-10-09T15:55:20.093Z",
    "message": "I have run into an issue. When trying to resize  the icons, they seem to lose some of their properties and don't look as nice after resizing. I feel like I am doing something wrong. I am copying and pasting the icons from the original project into mine, but when I click and drag to expand, they lose their properties and revert to basic SVGs. Please help.\n\n-Edit I figured out the issue. For the edit-alt icon, the pencil eraser is colored in with a trapezoid vector which at larger sizes, the corners bleed through the outline. If you need to resize these icons, be prepared for some extra steps.",
    "message_meta": [
     {
      "t": "I have run into an issue. When trying to resize  the icons, they seem to lose some of their properties and don't look as nice after resizing. I feel like I am doing something wrong. I am copying and pasting the icons from the original project into mine, but when I click and drag to expand, they lose their properties and revert to basic SVGs. Please help.\n\n-Edit I figured out the issue. For the edit-alt icon, the pencil eraser is colored in with a trapezoid vector which at larger sizes, the corners bleed through the outline. If you need to resize these icons, be prepared for some extra steps."
     }
